+summary: Build each agent request as a byte-identical static prefix followed by an append-only history,
+  so every turn reads the prompt cache instead of reprocessing it. Put identity, rules and tool definitions
+  before the cache boundary and anything that changes (date, state, memory, mode, settings) after it as
+  appended messages; serialize deterministically; send earlier turns back verbatim, thinking blocks included
+  where the model keeps them; check the provider's caching minimum (a prefix below it never caches); and
+  track per-turn cache misses, since 108 of 120 fixed caching defects in ten open-source agents raised
+  no error. Against a prefix broken on every call, caching cut cost 41-80% and time to first token 6-31%
+  on one research benchmark, and in one inference provider's traffic a change to the tool list or reasoning
+  effort made a cache break more than 20 times as likely. The evidence is small and covers cost and latency,
+  not quality; caching the whole context raised latency on one model, and a cache shared across customers
+  lets them test whether a known prompt was sent.
+how: '1. Start from the baseline: log per request the cache read, cache write and uncached input tokens
+  (on Claude: cache_read_input_tokens, cache_creation_input_tokens, input_tokens), a hash of the tools,
+  system prompt and messages, and where the request first differs from the previous one, or the provider''s
+  cache-miss reason (Anthropic''s cache diagnostics names whether the model, system prompt, tools or messages
+  diverged). Compute the token-weighted hit rate per session and the cost of each avoidable miss, and
+  check the meter itself: 23 of 120 fixed caching defects in ten open-source agents miscounted cache tokens.
+  2. Read the prompt assembly code and order content by how often it changes: tool definitions and static
+  instructions first, then project or session content, then the growing history. Keep the system prompt
+  byte-stable, with no timestamp, request or session id, git status or memory in it (a live timestamp
+  there meant the cache never hit); put per-turn values after the history as an appended message that
+  supersedes earlier ones, keep the date to the day and fixed for the session, and announce a date change
+  with an appended note. 3. Make the bytes deterministic: rebuild each request from an append-only session
+  log so retries and resumes are byte-identical; sort keys in tool schemas and tool-call JSON (some languages
+  randomize key order) and avoid random per-request ids; keep the tool list sorted and identical in every
+  mode, appending new tools at the end, since a tool inserted mid-list re-reads everything after it (to
+  restrict tools without editing the list, see 3.b.ii); send assistant turns and tool results back verbatim.
+  Keep thinking out of persisted history only where the provider does not expect it back (as Gemini CLI
+  does); on Claude models that keep prior thinking (Opus 4.5 and later, Sonnet 4.6 and later, Haiku 5.5),
+  pass thinking blocks back unmodified, because a dropped block changes the cached prefix from that point
+  on. 4. Mark the boundary to fit the provider. Put the cache breakpoint on the last block that is identical
+  across requests, never on the block that varies: on Claude, writes happen only at breakpoints, reads
+  look back at most 20 blocks and up to 4 breakpoints are allowed, so add an intermediate one when a turn
+  appends 20 or more blocks, or use automatic caching on an append-only history. Do not assume caching
+  everything is best: in one study with a 10,000-token system prompt, caching the full context raised
+  GPT-4o''s time to first token 8.8% where caching only the stable system prompt cut it 30.9% (cost differed
+  by 2-4 points across placements), so compare placements on your own provider and session lengths. Enable
+  caching through a capability lookup, not model-name checks (37 of the 120 defects silently lost caching
+  when a model was renamed or added). Confirm the static prefix clears the model''s minimum (512 to 4,096
+  tokens across current Claude models; below it nothing caches and no error is returned). Choose the lifetime
+  from the gap between turns: Claude''s default is 5 minutes from the start of the request, refreshed
+  on each hit, with writes at 1.25x input; 1-hour writes cost 2x and pay when turns or side agents run
+  5 to 60 minutes apart. Keep the model fixed within a cached conversation (caches are per model; see
+  1.b.i), and send one stable cache key or session id per conversation where the API routes by one. 5.
+  Keep settings, modes and compaction from rewriting the prefix. Settle reasoning effort and thinking
+  settings per session, or carry a change in an appended message where the API allows it: two open-model
+  chat templates write effort at token 8, and on Claude a thinking or top-level effort change restarts
+  the cache while a per-message effort change does not. Put mode reminders in their own appended message
+  (a plan-mode reminder edited into and out of the user message re-read 330 to 2,340 tokens a turn) and
+  do not prune or replace earlier history in place each turn (one replacement re-read 5,846 of 15,520
+  tokens). Compact late, running the summarizer on the conversation''s exact prefix with the instruction
+  appended rather than over a re-serialized transcript (22% cached in the largest such workload one provider
+  saw). Run forks and sub-agents that share the parent''s context the same way, and for parallel calls
+  on a shared prefix send the rest after the first response starts, since a Claude cache entry exists
+  only from then. 6. If several customers share one provider credential (a relay, gateway or shared workspace),
+  keep their cache state apart: carry a namespace derived from the authenticated customer into every cache
+  lookup and write, or split after a verified public prefix. Under a shared credential five of five open-source
+  gateways exposed cross-customer cache reads; the split kept most reuse at a modeled 1.7 to 2.5% cost
+  increase, against 2.29 to 3.14 times for full separation. 7. Measure: replay the hand-labeled set (or
+  recorded sessions with the date fixed) before and after, plus scripted sessions that switch mode, change
+  effort and back, connect and disconnect a tool server, add a skill, cross midnight, idle past the cache
+  lifetime, restart and resume, spawn a sub-agent and compact; confirm outputs and task success are unchanged,
+  and compare token-weighted cache read share, cost per task, time to first token by context depth and
+  the first divergence position, per model and provider. In production, alert on hit-rate drops and on
+  deep turns that re-read most of the prompt: 108 of the 120 defects raised no error.'
