-summary: 'On a bounded corpus (up to about 100K documents), grep and file reads over the raw text beat
-  an embedding retriever: the agent narrows into documents it has found. As the corpus grows, grep degrades
-  (37.5% at 400K); add semantic search beside it, and on large codebases semantic search plus grep beats
-  grep alone. A dense retriever beats BM25. Use a knowledge-graph retriever only for multi-hop and synthesis
-  questions, routed per query; keep chunk retrieval for single-fact lookup, return source text with any
-  graph triplets, and avoid global community-summary search for detail questions.'
