+caveats: 'Almost all the corpus-size evidence comes from one benchmark (BrowseComp-Plus: hard multi-constraint
+  questions over 100,195 long web pages, padded with random web pages to scale), mostly on 100-question
+  subsets in single runs, and the two scaling studies share an author, so the crossover may sit elsewhere
+  for paraphrase-heavy, multilingual or private corpora; short passages tolerated grep at 21M documents.
+  BM25 against dense is confounded by the harness: the tuned-BM25 result compares a new agent with published
+  dense runs, inside one harness dense still led slightly (82 against 80 of 100), and one study found
+  that adding either retriever beside grep lowered accuracy on 200 questions (88.5% to 84.0% and 78.5%),
+  though embeddings edged ahead on a 100-question rerun (90.0 against 89.0). The code evidence is a vendor''s
+  own benchmark and one study of 0.6B to 32B open models scored on localization only with a 0.6B embedder,
+  so the gain for frontier coding models is untested outside the vendor''s claim. The graph results come
+  from two 2025 papers with small routing gains, and the long-context comparison gave the full-context
+  model only a random 100K-token sample on corpus tasks, so it does not test reading a whole corpus in
+  context.'
