+summary: 'Keep a long task''s plan, progress, decisions and large results in files, and start every new
+  context window by reading them back. In measured studies, mostly of deep-research, coding and autoresearch
+  agents, state kept outside the history beat a growing or compacted one: Anthropic''s memory tool plus
+  context editing gained 39% on agentic search against 29% for context editing alone, a checkpoint of
+  progress and verified facts plus a self-chosen reset took Claude Sonnet 4 from 22.7% to 30.7% on 150
+  BrowseComp questions with the same tools, and fresh contexts over the same workspace beat one compacted
+  session at equal compute (0.55 against 0.45 normalized score). Form matters: a structured handoff beat
+  a narrative summary of the same length (52.1% against 42.8% of tasks fully completed, GPT-5.4), and
+  state updated by code answered access questions at 0.80 where a ledger the model rewrote itself fell
+  to chance. The limits: the full history still beat a compact handoff where it fit, a strong reasoning
+  model needed explicit state only for long histories, a 7B model lost accuracy with the extra tools,
+  and stale, wrong or unread notes misled agents, so enforce read-back, let code apply updates, measure
+  per model, and within one window use a re-injected task list (7.b.iv) instead.'
