-  step, until it answers or hits a cap. The loop is the common default for tasks that need several dependent
-  tool calls; the 2022 text template (Thought/Action/Observation lines in a few-shot prompt) is not. On
-  current models, use native tool calling, carry the model''s reasoning across tool calls, bound the whole
-  feedback path, and keep the per-step preamble small: with the model fixed, the harness around the loop
-  moved cost per task by up to 3x and pass rate by less than the noise.'
-how: '1. Use the provider''s native tool calling, not a text Thought/Action/Observation template. 2. Loop:
-  call the model, run every tool call it returns, append each result to the history (errors included,
-  as observations), and call again; stop on a final answer or an explicit finish tool. 3. Let the model
-  reason before each action (interleaved or adaptive thinking; a think tool on models without it), and
-  pass its reasoning back unchanged across tool calls. 4. Cap steps, cost and wall time on the whole feedback
-  path, retries and handoffs included; count a cap hit as a failure (7.b.iii sizes the caps, 7.b.i catches stalls).
-  5. Keep the per-step preamble (system prompt and tool schemas) small; it is re-sent every step. 6. Paired
