+  sparingly'' also cut needed calls (8.4 points of accuracy), asking for a necessity check before acting
+  collapsed two Llama models'' tool calling (Llama-3.1-8B 79.5% to 31.2%) while a per-skill YES/NO check
+  took Sonnet 4.5 to 100% activation, and a scope instruction that restored answers on four models cut
+  another''s needed tool use from 94.4% to 72.4%. A rule''s gain may not come from its content: random
+  CLAUDE.md rule files raised Opus 4.6''s pass rate as much as curated ones (63.8% each against 50.0%),
+  though another study found same-length unrelated text had no effect on rule compliance, and VeRO''s
+  tool-instruction edit lost 5 points on MATH while its SimpleQA gain is bundled with description changes.
+  Rules do not create tool use a model lacks: weak models barely searched when told to (BrowseComp-Plus),
