+caveats: 'Most of the new evidence is one study per design, often by the method''s own authors: the validator-governed
+  runtime''s gains include online feedback and repair with one run per task, the critic comparison used
+  about 30 tasks per benchmark with three trials and no confidence intervals, and the dialogue-only check
+  was tested on small or older models over public tau2-bench tasks. Checks err both ways: the dialogue-only
+  check withheld 17% and 41% of correct runs, letting unqualified validators block lost 9.7% of the tasks
+  the unguarded agent had passed (3.2% with qualified ones), gates that reopened the work cost some models
+  up to 10.7 points and once turned a passing result into a failure, and a guard that only refused to
+  stop finished none of the work-unit tasks without progress tracking. LLM checkers can still be swayed
+  by agent-written content in the state or trace, and the fault-injection suites behind their best numbers
+  are their authors'' own. Rules and tests the agent can see or edit stay weak (forbidding test weakening
+  left 4 of 6 models below no protection), so the check helps only where the agent cannot reach it (9.a.i).'
